  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "The sides of a triangle are \\(25,\\) \\(39,\\) and \\(40.\\) The diameter of the circumscribed circle is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{133}{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{125}{3}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(42\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(41\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(40\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "125/3"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1959-p43.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The semiperimeter is \\(52,\\) so Heron’s formula gives \\[ K=\\sqrt{52\\cdot27\\cdot13\\cdot12}=468. \\] If \\(R\\) is the circumradius, then \\[ R=\\frac{25\\cdot39\\cdot40}{4\\cdot468}=\\frac{125}{6}. \\] Hence the diameter is \\(2R=\\frac{125}{3}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Use Heron’s formula with semiperimeter \\(52\\)",
        "After finding the area \\(K,\\) use \\(abc=4KR\\) and double the circumradius"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
